# Phase 5 evidence and golden vectors carry a SHA-256 digest of their own raw
# bytes, recorded inside a companion JSON manifest and checked by
# hardware/simulation/scripts/phase5_tools.py (validate-evidence,
# validate-site-evidence) and hardware/protocol/scripts/generate_vectors.py.
#
# Without this file, a contributor's local `core.autocrlf=true` (the common
# Windows Git default) silently rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, changing the
# file's bytes and invalidating every recorded hash — with no error until the
# validator is actually run. `-text` disables that conversion unconditionally,
# on every platform and every local core.autocrlf setting, so a fresh clone
# always reproduces exactly the bytes that were committed and hashed.
hardware/evidence/generated/** -text
hardware/simulation/site-planner/study-input.json -text
hardware/protocol/vectors/** -text
